comment author Shinryuu
comment v5.8: v5.7 with one lag frame removed in the Heat Man refight. On the frame Heat Man's second fireball lands and spawns a fire pillar, Mega Man has turned left and gives no input, so that frame finishes in time; he holds A one frame longer in the jump before it, so his landing sound starts on the same music frame as in v5.7. He ends up 4 pixels behind, which changes no hit, and two re-timed steps on the walk to the exit keep the exit; the kill, the exit and everything after come 1 frame earlier. v5.7: v5.6 with the Quick Man refight fill 4 frames earlier. The Wily 2 boss is now beaten with 39 Metal Blades instead of 42 (two blocks are killed by parked stationary blades; the Wily 2 end is on the same frame), which saves the Metal Blade unit a faster Bubble Man refight needs: Bubble Man dies 5 frames sooner with 8 blades, every hit at the 19-frame minimum (two stationary blades in his path, and one extra blade holding slot 4 so the last three hits land on slot 3). The Quick Man refight keeps its pattern with three re-timed steps (Mega Man's subpixel for the boss's random jumps); one extra Air Shooter shot on the hub walk to the Crash capsule restores the tornado slot subpixels the Crash Man refight needs; the Metal capsule is entered with a re-picked subpixel so Metal Man still makes his low jump; three Wily Machine Metal Blade throws change direction so every hit stays on its frame and the Wily 6 platform seeds stay in range. v5.6: v5.5 with one lag frame removed in Bubble Man's stage: an A press removes a lag in the second spike zip, Mega Man stays in the water one frame longer, and one extra frame in the Metal Blade menu puts the DelayDownScroll check back on a heavy music frame; the Bubble Man fill then ends 1 frame earlier with the same frame counter. v5.5: v5.4 with the Metal Man refight fill 4 frames earlier: the Crash Man refight is 1 frame faster (the second Air Shooter volley comes 1 frame earlier from a different jump, so the second hit lands on slot 4 and the kill on slot 3 one frame sooner) and the hub pause uses the up+down menu trick; the Metal capsule is entered with a re-picked subpixel so Metal Man still makes his low jump, and the Flash capsule walk is re-timed; two Wily Machine Metal Blade throws turned up-right keep every hit on the same frame with the new stale subpixels and the Wily 6 platform seeds in range. v5.4: both Wily Machine fights faster (Wily 6 starts 8 frames earlier). v5.3: alien fight 2 frames faster (pause-menu up+down cursor trick flips the hit parity; Mega Man ends his stun at X 37.06 on the secret ledge). v5.2: one lag frame removed before Wily 4 (Mega Man hops into Metal Man's boss door). v5.1: combined movie. Shinryuu's unpublished, faster run (reconstructed from his video) from the start to Wily 4, combined with our improvements (v3 Guts Tank fight, v4.1 Wily 4, v4.2 Wily 5/6) and two Wily 5 refight levers: the Air Man refight is 11 frames faster (Leaf Shield deployed right after the first hit and thrown while Mega Man rises, between the tornado rows), so the Wood Man fill ends 12 frames earlier; the Metal Man refight is 2 frames faster and the Flash capsule is reached 1 frame sooner, so the Flash Man fill ends 4 frames earlier. Refight RNG re-synced through capsule subpixels; Wily 6 platform seeds set with Metal Blade knobs. 260 frames faster than publication 4410.
